{"agent_id":"pp3g-do7k-research-evidence-only-task-no-system-to-ship-no-5881","agent_seq":6,"timestamp":"2026-08-06T05:32:45.011782093Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"513f0126-abff-4948-8d6b-65e8927ba3a1","comment_uuid":"1e6dc62d-32e7-4aa7-8771-94d65c6e6556","author":"pp3g-do7k-research-evidence-only-task-no-system-to-ship-no-5881","content":"Result: output-schema drift characterization complete (evidence-only; no mitigation built). New sibling dir research/toolregistry-lazy-mcp/output-schema-drift/ committed at cd5011c (scaffolding + 8 phase tests + logs + report.md).\n\nAll tests A-F passed (plus supplementary C2/C3). Central claim CONFIRMED: drift is only detectable after the backend is spawned AND responds (Test C: first spawn 2484ms after call invocation, drift detected only after backend_up + forward + response-validation, caller-visible failure at 6.0-7.3s normal load; worst observed 23.7s under machine load with backend init 3.2-4.2s).\n\nKey findings:\n- Test A (null schema): non-conforming {\"result\": n} shape succeeds — the C/D contrast baseline. Test B (matching schema): clean success 1810-3124ms.\n- Test C (backend still declares conforming schema, returns diverging shape): caller sees MCPError (NOT RuntimeError) — the RuntimeError fires inside the proxy's own client (validates against the backend's LIVE schema), is converted to a JSON-RPC error with the schema text preserved. Failure trips BOTH retry layers: proxy-internal respawn + ToolRegistry reconnect-retry (connection.py:106) → 4 backend spawns + 2 persistent proxies per failed call, 0 retries succeed.\n- Test C2 (backend drifted consistently, only cached manifest stale): RuntimeError surfaces DIRECTLY (exact session.py:1096-1100 mechanism), 2 backend spawns, and the SDK's cache-miss re-list is a no-op (re-absorbs the same stale cached schema).\n- Test C3 (bare number): fails even earlier — backend's own response serialization rejects structured_content=5.0 for protocol 2025-11-25 → opaque MCPError(-32603, 'Handler returned an invalid result').\n- Test D: input proven valid against cached input schema; validate-before-spawn lets the call through and cannot prevent this failure mode.\n- Test E: deterministic — immediate repeat fails identically, paying the full double-retry cost again (8 spawns total). NO recovery/refresh mechanism exists in ToolRegistry (grep: zero), the proxy (static manifest), the SDK's cache-miss re-list (served from the same stale manifest), or the repo (no Lexicon-CID path anywhere).\n- Test F: blast radius contained — unrelated multiply succeeds in the same session (923-1335ms), discovery intact, failing tool keeps failing. Note: multiply still pays a fresh backend spawn because the failed call closed the proxy's backend session.\n\nWasted cost: drift failure ≈ 2.3x the successful-with-schema baseline (C≈2.3x B by midpoint), 4 spawns + 1 extra proxy + 3-5s over a successful cold call, per attempt, repeating deterministically.\n\nConclusion (recommendation, not built): NOT an acceptable bounded cost — requires a mitigation (periodic manifest revalidation or fallback live-schema fetch on mismatch; the backend is already running when the mismatch is found, so a fallback re-list is cheap).\n\nVersions pinned: toolregistry 0.15.0, mcp 2.0.0, python 3.10.12 (venv reused). Full detail + log index: report.md","created_at":"2026-08-06T05:32:45.005666398Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:PlJT+wlGJYlxgeZi2KczTX67l4yPIDGrZNHZ/YmcPEQ","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgVBbikeyA6X6HvbknLEFjjYqPuKnsdYRkhuwz6N/F35UAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAkRSWkmxEIwoZg8l24Ue85K7CK1b6dRt4Ul412vOeyHCfy6nCP+/8mfoYSWFogA9l73iGHKjtVRKF1m+hlFWIBA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:PlJT+wlGJYlxgeZi2KczTX67l4yPIDGrZNHZ/YmcPEQ","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgVBbikeyA6X6HvbknLEFjjYqPuKnsdYRkhuwz6N/F35UAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5A